Title: F1-M10 — A Quiet Horizon (briefing)
Credit: Staalfront
Author: Staalfront narrative team
Draft date: 2026-10-17

> FADE IN:

INT. FOUNDRY RUIN OBSERVATION POST - PRE-DAWN

[[AMBIENCE: wind through broken brick, dripping water, a generator far below]]
[[MUSIC: low, resolved tension]]

A plan of the control centre is weighted down with spent shell cases on a slab of fallen masonry. CAPTAIN ELIAN and MIRA stand over it.

MIRA
(serious)
Intercepts show the regional command centre is preparing one final offensive. Its archive contains the original deployment orders.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(measured)
The archive is more important than the buildings around it. We need proof, not ruins.

[[SHOT: map]]
[[MAP: terrace base with three ore fields, west road and gate, canal path to the overlook, marshalling yard north-east, inner wall and platform, data room, generator and command relay at the centre]]

MIRA
(firm)
Secure the data room before the evacuation protocol wipes it. Stop the offensive and recover the records.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(short)
Six thousand credits, full roster. Everything we have learned goes in tonight.

MIRA
(dry)
The marshalling yard is fuelling heavy armour now. Fifteen minutes, by their own intercepts. Kill the yard or meet the column at our south gate.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(pointing at map)
Siege guns to the canal overlook. They outrange the gate defences. Engineers stay in the transport until the inner wall is open.

MIRA
(analytical)
Once we are inside the inner wall, the centre will know. I do not know what it does then. A building that holds this much paper will not simply hand it over.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(neutral)
No shells near the archive. Not one.

MIRA
(resolute)
If the orders in that room were written here, the war is theirs. If they were not, somebody has been writing to both of us.

[[SFX: radio click]]
[[MUSIC: stop]]

> FADE OUT.
